---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../lib/brand';
---

<Layout title="Docs · Baken" description="Install, pair, and understand Baken's local-first agent architecture and living Rive motion system.">
  <section class="docs-wrap">
    <div class="container wrap docs-inner">
      <header class="docs-plate">
        <div class="docs-plate-art" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="docs-plate-meta">
          <span>PLATE IX · DOCUMENTATION</span>
          <span>Boussole des vents · P. Mortier · c. 1702 · RP-P-OB-83.034-278</span>
        </div>
      </header>
      <h1>Getting started with Baken</h1>
      <p class="docs-lead">
        Baken is a client for persistent AI agents. Your agents run on a host machine you control, and the Android and desktop apps pair with it over an encrypted peer-to-peer connection.
      </p>

      <div class="doc-block" id="install">
        <h2>1. Download &amp; Install</h2>
        <p>
          The download page links straight to the right file for your device: the Android APK, the Windows installer, the Linux AppImage and the host wrapper. There is no macOS or iOS build yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={LINKS.download}>
            Go to downloads →
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          <strong>Note during the rename to Baken:</strong> some release files still carry older names. The Android APKs are <code>letta-mobile-*.apk</code> and the host wrapper is <code>meridian-iroh-wrapper-*.tar</code>. The <a href={LINKS.releases} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">latest-release page</a> always has the newest build.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block" id="pairing">
        <h2>2. Pair your devices (QR over Iroh)</h2>
        <p>
          Baken connects to your agent host over Iroh. The connection is encrypted end to end and goes direct when it can, falling back to a relay that cannot read the traffic. You don't need a public reverse proxy or hand-copied API tokens.
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Start letta-code and the Baken host wrapper on your Linux or Windows machine.</li>
          <li>Generate a pairing invite QR code from the CLI or Desktop host.</li>
          <li>Scan from Baken on Android to establish a mutually authenticated peer connection.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block" id="motion">
        <h2>3. Brand Mark &amp; Mascot Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing in Baken is static, and no two indicators compete. Both <code>baken-mark.riv</code> and <code>mascot.riv</code> compile through the same Rive ViewModel pipeline and honor system <code>reduceMotion</code>.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Asset</th>
              <th>Role</th>
              <th>States Owned</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>baken-mark.riv</code></td>
              <td>App / Harbour / Connection</td>
              <td><code>idle</code>, <code>boot</code>, <code>loading</code> (hydration only), <code>connecting</code>, <code>degraded</code>, <code>ambient</code>, <code>success</code> (peer lock)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>mascot.riv</code></td>
              <td>Per-agent presence &amp; turns</td>
              <td><code>listening</code>, <code>thinking</code>, <code>working</code>, <code>waitingInput</code>, <code>speaking</code>, <code>dreaming</code>, <code>sleeping</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>dragged</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block" id="open-source">
        <h2>4. Repositories</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={LINKS.appRepo} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>Client &amp; runtime</strong> — <code>oculairmedia/letta-mobile</code></a></li>
          <li><a href={LINKS.webRepo} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><strong>Website</strong> — <code>oculairmedia/baken-web</code></a> (Astro on Cloudflare Workers)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs-wrap { padding: 44px 0 96px; position: relative; z-index: 3; }
  .docs-inner { max-width: 760px; }
  .docs-plate {
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .docs-plate-art {
    height: 156px;
    width: 100%;
    background-color: var(--tone-ochre);
    -webkit-mask-image: url('/art/boussole-des-vents-1702.png'), linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,1) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.88) 72%, rgba(0,0,0,0.22) 100%);
            mask-image: url('/art/boussole-des-vents-1702.png'), linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,1) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.88) 72%, rgba(0,0,0,0.22) 100%);
    -webkit-mask-size: cover, 100% 100%;
            mask-size: cover, 100% 100%;
    -webkit-mask-position: center 50%, 0 0;
            mask-position: center 50%, 0 0;
    -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
            mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    -webkit-mask-composite: source-in;
            mask-composite: intersect;
  }
  .docs-plate-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 9px 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'JetBrains Mono', SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: clamp(36px, 4.8vw, 52px); letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.06; }
  .docs-lead { font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 48px; }
  .doc-block {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 36px 0;
  }
  .doc-block h2 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 22px; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .doc-block p, .doc-block li { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .doc-block strong, .doc-block a:not(.btn) { color: var(--text); }
  .doc-block a:not(.btn):hover { color: var(--stone-2); }
  .doc-block code {
    font-size: 13px;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .note {
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 13.5px !important;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 12px 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  th { color: var(--text); font-weight: 700; }
</style>
